<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>He healeth me! my simple faith</l><l>Believes the word that Jesus saith,</l><l>And takes the place of ardent hope,</l><l>Believes the Lord will raise me up.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>He healeth me! I touch for cure</l><l>The border of His garment pure,</l><l>And virtue through my being flows,</l><l>A healing balm for nature’s woes.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>He healeth me, as when of yore,</l><l>Their sins and sicknesses He bore;</l><l>Nor has He lost His power and skill—</l><l>Our blessed Christ is living still.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>He healeth me! how oft I sought</l><l>This healing power, but found it not:</l><l>But now I trust with all my soul,</l><l>And now through faith He makes me whole.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
